Description: pco: reindex instructions after preproc_vecs() copies vec sources
 preproc_vecs() gives every vec use of an SSA value that feeds more than one
 vec its own mbyp copy. A new instruction takes func->next_instr++ as its
 index, so the copy sorts behind every instruction of the function. The pass
 only reindexed for the >4-channel path (vec merge), not for these copies.
 pco_ra_func() then computes live ranges from the stale indices: a vec whose
 coalesced source is such a copy starts after its own last use, interferes
 with nothing and can share registers with values that are still live.
 .
 Seen in dEQP-VK.renderpasses.renderpass{1,2}.*.attachment.8.797: the vec for
 the R16G16_SFLOAT pack of attachment 7 got the registers of an earlier vec
 whose component it still had to read, the copy of its first source
 overwrote that component and the pack wrote the red value into green.
 .
 Set needs_reindex for the copy path as well.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
